Description: Return the screen to the Overview tab after a successful load
 On a CDJ/XDJ you browse, hit LOAD, and the unit puts the deck back in front
 of you; the Pioneered skin left you sitting in the Browse (or Search) tab
 after the track was on the deck, so every load needed a second tap on the
 Overview tab to see the waveform you had just loaded.
 .
 WTrackTableView::loadSelectedTrackToGroup now sets the skin's Overview
 WidgetStack trigger once the load has actually been emitted -- exactly the
 control a tap on the Overview tab writes.
 .
 Placement is the whole point: it sits after every rejection path in the
 function, so a load that did *not* happen leaves you where you were.
 In particular a deck that is still playing the previous track takes the
 early return added by usb-force-eject.patch (which raises
 [Library],load_blocked and shows the "PAUSE DECK TO LOAD" banner) and never
 reaches this line -- the browser stays up, with your place in the list and
 the banner explaining why, instead of the view jumping away from a load
 that was refused. The same holds for an empty selection and for a row the
 model has no track for.
 .
 Preview decks are excluded: previewing a track is a browsing action, so it
 must not throw you out of the browser.
 .
 [Tab],overview is a skin-defined control -- LegacySkinParser creates it for
 the SingletonContainer trigger of the Overview page. Skins that do not
 define it (stock Mixxx skins) simply have no such control, and
 ControlObject::set() on a missing key is a no-op, so this is inert
 everywhere but Pioneered. This mirrors the existing [Library],load_blocked
 write a few lines above.
Author: Pioneered CI <pioneered-build@localhost>
Forwarded: no

--- a/src/widget/wtracktableview.cpp
+++ b/src/widget/wtracktableview.cpp
@@ -1404,6 +1404,21 @@ void WTrackTableView::loadSelectedTrackToGroup(const QString& group, bool play)
     TrackPointer pTrack;
     if (pTrackModel && (pTrack = pTrackModel->getTrack(index))) {
         emit loadTrackToPlayer(pTrack, group, play);
+        // XDJ: the load happened, so put the deck back in front of the user
+        // the way a CDJ does. Every way this function can refuse a load --
+        // empty selection, a deck still playing the previous track (the
+        // load_blocked early return above), a row with no track -- returns
+        // before this point, so a refused load leaves the browser up with
+        // its banner and the user's place in the list.
+        //
+        // [Tab],overview is the Pioneered skin's WidgetStack trigger for the
+        // Overview page; writing 1 to it is precisely what tapping the
+        // Overview tab does, including clearing the Browse/Search triggers
+        // via their on_hide_select. Skins without that container never
+        // create the control and ControlObject::set() is then a no-op.
+        if (!PlayerManager::isPreviewDeckGroup(group)) {
+            ControlObject::set(ConfigKey("[Tab]", "overview"), 1.0);
+        }
     }
 }
 
